# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nucouths — Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to .env (or .env.local) and fill in real values. Never
# commit the actual .env file — it's already covered by .gitignore's env
# patterns. This is a template only; no real credentials belong here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# [SERVER-ONLY, REQUIRED] PostgreSQL connection string used by Prisma
# (prisma.config.ts's datasource.url, read via lib/prisma.ts's PrismaPg
# adapter). Never sent to the browser.
#
# On Supabase specifically: use the SESSION pooler connection string (port
# 5432, host like aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com), not the TRANSACTION
# pooler (port 6543). Session mode behaves like a normal Postgres
# connection — it supports Prisma's prepared statements and works for both
# application queries and `prisma migrate deploy`/`db:migrate` with no
# extra config. The transaction-mode pooler (6543) does NOT support
# prepared statements without adding `?pgbouncer=true` to the URL, and
# generally needs a separate, non-pooled DIRECT_URL for migrations — don't
# switch to it without also adding that.
# Format: postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DATABASE?schema=public
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/nucouths?schema=public"

# [SERVER-ONLY, REQUIRED] Razorpay API key pair (lib/razorpay.ts). Use TEST
# MODE keys (rzp_test_...) from your Razorpay dashboard during development,
# LIVE MODE keys (rzp_live_...) only in production — lib/razorpay.ts's
# assertRazorpayKeyMatchesEnvironment() now refuses to start a payment flow
# if RAZORPAY_KEY_ID's mode doesn't match NODE_ENV (a live key outside
# production, or a test key in production, throws instead of silently
# proceeding). KEY_ID is technically the public half of the pair — Razorpay
# Checkout needs it client-side, and lib/razorpay.ts's getRazorpayKeyId()
# is the one function that hands it to the browser — but it still lives
# here as a server env var, not NEXT_PUBLIC_*, since it's only ever read
# server-side and returned through a Server Action response, never bundled
# into client JS. KEY_SECRET never leaves the server at all (used only for
# the Orders API's Basic Auth and the Checkout payment-signature check) and
# must never be committed.
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID="rzp_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxx"
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET="your_test_key_secret"

# [SERVER-ONLY, REQUIRED] Razorpay WEBHOOK secret — a SEPARATE value from
# KEY_SECRET above, set when you create the webhook in the Razorpay
# dashboard (Settings -> Webhooks -> Add New Webhook, pointed at
# .../api/webhooks/razorpay, with the payment.captured and payment.failed
# events enabled). Razorpay shows you this secret once, at creation time —
# copy it here. Used only to verify the X-Razorpay-Signature header on
# incoming webhook requests (lib/razorpay.ts's
# verifyRazorpayWebhookSignature); never sent to the browser, never reused
# as RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET.
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET="your_webhook_secret"

# [SERVER-ONLY, OPTIONAL] lib/order-expiration.ts — how long an
# online-payment (upi/card/netbanking) Order may sit at
# paymentStatus=Pending before it's treated as abandoned and its reserved
# stock/coupon usage is released. COD orders are never affected (their
# Pending state just means "unpaid until delivery"). Defaults to 30 if
# unset or invalid.
PENDING_ORDER_EXPIRY_MINUTES="30"

# [SERVER-ONLY, REQUIRED] Shared secret for POST/GET
# /api/cron/expire-pending-orders — this is NOT a customer or admin
# session; it's the only auth an external scheduler (Hostinger Cron Jobs,
# or any other) presents when it calls that endpoint periodically. Generate
# a long random value (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`) and never commit it.
# Without this set, the endpoint always rejects every request rather than
# accepting unauthenticated ones.
CRON_SECRET="a-long-random-string"

# [SERVER-ONLY, REQUIRED] Session-signing secrets (lib/auth/session.ts,
# lib/admin/auth/session.ts) — HMAC keys for the customer and admin
# httpOnly session cookies. REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION: with
# NODE_ENV=production, a missing secret makes every session sign/verify
# call throw rather than silently fall back to a known value — sessions
# simply won't work until this is set. In development, an unset secret
# falls back to a random value generated once per process (existing
# sessions reset on restart) so local dev doesn't require these. Generate
# each with e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`. Keep them distinct from each
# other, and from CRON_SECRET/RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET — never reuse a
# secret across purposes. Never sent to the browser.
CUSTOMER_SESSION_SECRET="a-long-random-string-for-customer-sessions"
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET="a-different-long-random-string-for-admin-sessions"

# [SERVER-ONLY, REQUIRED] Supabase Storage — where admin-uploaded product
# and banner images are persisted (lib/admin/supabase-storage.ts), instead
# of Hostinger's local disk, which doesn't survive a redeploy and isn't
# shared across instances. Both values come from your Supabase project
# dashboard (Project Settings -> API).
#
# SUPABASE_URL is the project's base URL (https://<project-ref>.supabase.co)
# — same project as DATABASE_URL above if you're using Supabase for
# Postgres too, but this is the REST/Storage endpoint, not the Postgres
# connection string, so it's a separate variable.
#
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY is the project's secret service-role API key —
# it bypasses Storage's row-level-security policies entirely. Never prefix
# it with NEXT_PUBLIC_, never send it to the browser, never log it, and
# never commit it. Requires a PUBLIC Supabase Storage bucket named
# "product-images" to already exist (Storage -> New bucket, toggle
# "Public bucket" on) — lib/admin/supabase-storage.ts uploads into it and
# hands back that bucket's public URL for the browser to load images from
# directly, with no signed URL/expiry to manage.
SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project-ref.supabase.co"
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="your-supabase-service-role-key"
